<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#composite-bow">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Composite bow</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A composite bow is a bow made from layers of wood, horn and sinew glued together, giving great power in a short length suitable for use on horseback. It was the principal weapon of steppe and Iranian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-archer">horse archers</a>. It was used by the armies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/median-empire">Median Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a>, among others.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/composite-bow.jpg" alt="Composite bow" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wellcome Collection · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Manchu_Archer_Wellcome_L0040987.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
